# S1a: the K64j extent program at ONE KV head per chip (the TP4 attention shape), watcher pass, on one card. The riskiest
# single item of the port: if the 0x23 program (tail + share) is illegal at one KV head the four-card profiles cannot attach.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card S2 window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/s2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled in by whoever drives
# the window (the graft directory and the graft binary digest of the one-card harnesses); every other value is final.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image S0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate): 10-25 min (one family, two starts, no timing; the container timeout is 45 min, the step limit 100 min).
# The harness runs its own pinned image and mounts this checkout's scripts as the code under test: it does not use the S0 image.
# Read the K64J_NKV1 verdict line: extent program 0x23 at G8B2 and 0x21 at G16B1 bit-equal to the compile-time twin on the
# poisoned table, and the watcher log with no error or assert lines.
C2_CARDS=pair
C2_ACTIONS=cardm
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-s2-1
C2_CARDM_HARNESS=optimisation/ttnn-op/k64j/run_card_b.sh
C2_CARDM_ARGS=--extents 2304 --starts 128,255 --seeds 0 --iterations 0 --no-legacy
C2_CARDM_ENV=K64J_HARNESS=nkv1_spike WATCHER=1 KOPGRAFT64=/home/thatch/opgraft-K64j EXPECT_TTNNCPP_SHA256=152951c1c0de5c9dfad2d62c295393a43b2ecf353965c55c709da7e539b975b7
